Subject: [PATCH] nss: queue data plane registration without a fixed host CPU

The ordered registration workqueue is unbound, but queue_work_on(1) still
indexes its per-CPU pool table with CPU 1. On a kernel booted with
nr_cpus=1 that CPU is not possible. The first firmware initialization IRQ
therefore dereferences an invalid pool pointer in __queue_work and panics.

Use queue_work so the workqueue core selects a valid pool. This preserves
the ordered workqueue and works with both single- and multi-CPU hosts.
Observed on MF297D Linux 6.18.60 through UDP netconsole.

---
--- a/nss_data_plane/nss_data_plane_common.c
+++ b/nss_data_plane/nss_data_plane_common.c
@@ -58,12 +58,12 @@
  */
 bool nss_data_plane_schedule_registration(void)
 {
-	if (!queue_work_on(1, nss_data_plane_workqueue, &nss_data_plane_work.work)) {
-		nss_warning("Failed to register data plane workqueue on core 1\n");
+	if (!queue_work(nss_data_plane_workqueue, &nss_data_plane_work.work)) {
+		nss_warning("Failed to queue data plane registration work\n");
 		return false;
 	}
 
-	nss_info("Register data plane workqueue on core 1\n");
+	nss_info("Queued data plane registration work\n");
 	return true;
 }
 
